# Test files contain synthetic secret patterns for detector testing.
# These are NOT real secrets — they are fixtures that match regex patterns.
**/*_test.go

# Verifier implementations contain API URL patterns that may match detectors.
internal/verifier/**

# Go module checksums — hash values can trigger false positives.
go.sum

# Documentation may contain example patterns.
docs/**

# Vendor dependencies.
vendor/**

# Example custom-rule fixtures contain regex patterns designed to look like
# real secrets, which is exactly what trips the generic/entropy detectors.
# Self-scan tradeoff: this repo does not run `leakwatch scan fs .` against
# itself in CI (see docs/05-ROADMAP.md), so nothing currently exercises the
# case where this exclusion is missing or the fixtures grow new noise.
# Adding a self-scan CI/dogfood step would let this exclusion's correctness
# be verified continuously instead of by manual review.
rules/**
